From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] motor (4.4.94): module parameters, no end switches, bind to ingenic,tcu_chn2

The 4.4.94 SDK motor.ko has compile-time pins (T31 board values) and a
platform driver named "tcu_chn2", but the T41 4.4 kernel registers the MFD
cell as "ingenic,tcu_chn2", so it never probed (no /dev/motor). Pins were
also not configurable, unlike the 3.10.14 motors-pp driver that
thingino-motors/S59motor expect.

- bind to "ingenic,tcu_chn2"
- module parameters hst1..4, vst1..4, hmin/hmax/vmin/vmax (-1 = none),
  hmaxstep/vmaxstep, invert_gpio_dir, nolimits, debug, tcu_channels,
  motor_switch_gpio (accepted, unused)
- without end switches (nolimits, or any switch pin -1): do not touch the
  hardwired pull-ups, no switch reads, RESET ioctl keeps hmaxstep/vmaxstep
  and centres, moves are soft-clamped to [0, max]

Tested on Cinnado D1 (T41NQ, PTZ): pan/tilt move, direction and position
repeatable, tcu irq ticks.
